// c02_missing_close_brace_si_block.exsc
//
// Case c02. The mistake: the `}` of an `si` block is missing, 3 lines up
// from EOF.
//
// Review reported: `8:1 EXS-E0202 unterminated construct` (file has 7
// lines), fix insert `}` at EOF. Verdict: "bad" -- no opener span (the `{`
// that is actually unterminated is never named); the fix compiles but
// silently moves the trailing `redde` into the `si` block.
//
// Reconstruction: byte-faithful on the structural claims. Counting from the
// first byte of `publica` below, this program is exactly 7 lines and is
// reported at line 8, col 1, EXS-E0202, with a fix inserting `}` at EOF --
// matching the review's line count and reported position. The review gives
// no explicit byte offset for this case, only "at EOF", which also matches.
// Applying the fix (verified) yields a file that compiles clean but folds
// the final `redde r;` inside the `si` block, exactly as D3 describes.

publica functio maxima(a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 {
    firma r: u64 = a;
    si a lt b {
        r = b;
        r = r;
    redde r;
}
